    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "10. Shooting Phase",
    "ruleNumber": "10.06",
    "order": 147,
    "anchor": "10.06",
    "summary": "An **[engaged](vsdata:core-rule/engagement-range)** unit that has not [Advanced](vsdata:core-rule/advance-move) this turn can shoot this way if it has at least 1 **[[CLOSE-QUARTERS]](vsdata:weapon-ability/close-quarters)** weapon or the unit is **MONSTER/VEHICLE**. Its models can target enemy units their unit is [engaged](vsdata:core-rule/engagement-range) with, and attacks follow [Making Attacks](vsdata:core-rule/making-attacks) (04).\n\nFor each attack by a **MONSTER/VEHICLE** model:\n\n- the **Hit roll** takes -1, unless the attack uses a **[[CLOSE-QUARTERS]](vsdata:weapon-ability/close-quarters)** weapon against a unit the firer’s unit is engaged with\n- a **[[BLAST]](vsdata:weapon-ability/blast)** weapon may still not target a unit the firer’s unit is engaged with\n\nEvery other model is limited to **[[CLOSE-QUARTERS]](vsdata:weapon-ability/close-quarters)** weapons and to targets engaged with its unit.\n\nFor the rest of the phase the unit may not begin an Action.",
